# Which model each agent runs on, overriding what its `agents/<role>.md` declares.
#
# Copy to `.cerebro/models.conf` **in the consumer repository** (not here — this submodule is shared
# by every consumer). Whether to commit it is the project's: tracked, every clone runs the fleet on
# the same models; listed in `.gitignore`, it is yours alone.
#
#     cp .claude/cerebro/models.conf.example .cerebro/models.conf
#
# Every launch reads it. Nothing needs restarting except the sessions themselves, and a session that
# is already up keeps the model it started with — this decides what the *next* one gets.
#
#     <agent-name | role | default>[@provider]   <model | ->   [effort]
#
# Most specific wins: an agent's own name, then its role, then `default`. A `--model` typed on the
# command line still beats the file. `-` as the model passes no `--model` at all, leaving the
# session on whatever the agent CLI itself defaults to. Omit the effort column to keep the one the
# agent definition declares.
#
# A key may name the agent CLI it is about. `planner' applies whichever CLI this fleet runs on;
# `planner@copilot' applies only when .cerebro/project.conf declares `agent_cli copilot'. The most
# specific key wins, and for one key the provider-scoped row beats the plain one:
#
#     <Name>@<provider>, <Name>, <role>@<provider>, <role>, default@<provider>, default
#
# A key naming a CLI cerebro does not know is warned about once and ignored; the session starts.
#
# The agent definitions declare Claude Code's model words (`model: opus'). On any other CLI they
# are ignored and no --model and no --effort are passed at all, so this file is where a Copilot
# fleet's models are chosen - and Copilot's ids are Copilot's own:
#
#     default@copilot      claude-opus-4.8
#     implementer@copilot  gpt-5-mini   medium
#     architect@copilot    gpt-5.5      high
#
# Copilot accepts a reasoning effort only for SOME models and refuses the launch outright for the
# rest, so an effort here is passed verbatim and a bad pairing fails loudly.
#
# Anything from a `#` to the end of a line is a comment, including after a setting:
#
#     planner   fable   high      # both, with a note about why
#
# Every line here is commented out: the file as shipped changes nothing.

# Everything on Opus, keeping each role's declared effort:
# default   opus

# Back to Fable for planning only, at its usual effort:
# planner   fable   high

# One of the two planners on something else, to compare them on the same queue:
# Beast     sonnet

# Cheap sweeps: Cerebro reads tools and relays what they say.
# orchestrator  haiku

# Whatever the session default is, no flag passed:
# Xavier    -
